permalink: _routes.json
---
{{--
    Which requests Cloudflare Pages hands to the Function in functions/index.js.

    Once a project has a Function, Pages routes every request through it unless
    told otherwise, which would put a Worker in front of a site that is 99%
    static files. One URL needs it, the root, so one URL is what this includes.
    Everything else is served straight from the asset store, as it was before.

    Named routes.blade.json and given a permalink because Jigsaw never writes a
    source path beginning with an underscore, and _routes.json is the name Pages
    looks for. It is the same trick source/index.blade.php uses to land on
    index.html rather than index/index.html.
--}}
{
    "version": 1,
    "include": ["/"],
    "exclude": []
}
